• The phrase "magical day" typically implies a sense of wonder, enchantment, or awe, which suggests that the wedding was a positive and memorable experience.
• The context of a wedding suggests that the speaker is likely referring to the wedding itself, rather than another aspect of the event.
• The tone of the phrase is overwhelmingly positive, which contradicts the idea that the wedding was dull and disappointing (option c).

